###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/CorrosionPotential
<https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/CorrosionPotential> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                       rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/CorrosionProperty> ;
                                                                       rdfs:label "Corrosion potential"@en ;
                                                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Describes the tendency of a material to release (lose) electrons in the presence of a elecotrolyte. During electrochemical reactions at corrosion potential (E_{corr}), the anodic and cathodic currents are equal in magnitude, and there will not be any net value of current to be measured. The corrosion potential is defined at the potential value where the anodic and cathodic reaction rates meet."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/CorrosionProperty
<https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/CorrosionProperty> rdf:type owl:Class ;
