<https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/GrainBoundarySegment> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                         rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/PlanarDefect> ;
                                                                         rdfs:label "Grain boundary segment"@en ;
                                                                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A grain boundary segment is an approximately coplanar segment/facet of a grain boundary. Each segment can for instance be parametrized by five macroscopic grain boundary parameters. Three parameters specify the misorientations of the adjoining and grain regions and two parameters determine the orientation of the boundary. Furthermore, there are further microscopic parameters."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/GrainRefinement
<https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/GrainRefinement> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                    rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/Mechanism> ;
                                                                    rdfs:label "Grain refinement"@en ;
                                                                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The mechanism by which the grain size is reduced through the introduction of particles (e.g. titanium or titanium–boron additions as grain refiners) which act as nucleation sites during recrystallization and grain boundary pinning sites during grain growth." ;
                                                                    <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/definitionSource> "GPT-4 generated description with manual adjustments" .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/GrainSize
