###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/HardnessTest
<https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/HardnessTest> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                 rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/MechanicalTest> ;
                                                                 rdfs:label "Hardness test"@en ;
                                                                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A mechanical test where an indentation is performed with defined indentation tools and a specific load to measure a specimen's resistance to indentation by optical measurement of the indentation cross-section."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/HardnessUnit
<https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/HardnessUnit> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                 rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/MechanicalProperty> ;
                                                                 rdfs:label "Hardness unit"@en ;
                                                                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Hardness is a measure of the resistance to localized plastic deformation induced by either mechanical identation. There are different types of units of measurement, such as Brinell (HB), Vickers (HV) or Rockwell (HR) resulting from different testing methods. Hardness values may be compared under certain conditions following DIN EN ISO 18265."@en .


