                                                                     rdfs:label "Interstitial atom"@en ;
                                                                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An additional atom at a position not part of the regular lattice but rather in free sites inside the unit cell."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/Intrusion
<https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/Intrusion> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                              rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/Damage> ;
                                                              rdfs:label "Intrusion"@en ;
                                                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A persistent slip marking which is local and resembles a notch is the surface. Typically, intrusions form where the transilition from a slip band to the matrix meets the surface."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/IsotropicHardening
<https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/IsotropicHardening> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                       rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/Mechanism> ;
                                                                       rdfs:label "Isotropic hardening"@en ;
