                                                                       <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/definitionSource> "GPT-4 generated description with manual adjustments" .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/KinematicViscosity
<https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/KinematicViscosity> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                       rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/MassMaterialsProperty> ;
                                                                       rdfs:label "Kinematic viscosity"@en ;
                                                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A measure of a fluid's internal resistance to flow under gravity." ;
                                                                       <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/definitionSource> "Description generated by GPT-4" .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/KneePoint
<https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/KneePoint> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                              rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/MechanicalProperty> ;
                                                              rdfs:label "Knee point"@en ;
                                                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Depending on the type of the SN-curve model, one or several knee points exist, where the SN curve changes its slope. For ferritic steels, there is usually a constant, non-zero slope of the SN-curve in the high cycle fatigue regime (e.g. 10^4 < n < 10^6), followed by a horizontal shape of the SN curve after reaching the fatigue strength / endurance limit. In this case the knee point corresponds to the endurance limit. For other materials (e.g. aluminium or austenitic steels), a horizontal slope is never reached, but there are at least two regions with different slope, which are separated by the knee point (in terms of cycles)."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/KnoopHardness
<https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/KnoopHardness> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                  rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/MechanicalProperty> ;
                                                                  rdfs:label "Knoop hardness"@en ;
                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A measure of hardness measuring the resistance of a material to indendation. Knoop microhardness testing is particularly applied for very brittle materials or thin sheets, where only a small indentation may be made for testing. The indenter tip is a diamond-shaped pyramid." ;
                                                                  <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/definitionSource> "GPT-4 generated description with manual adjustments" .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/LaserCutting
<https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/LaserCutting> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                 rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/MachiningProcess> ;
                                                                 rdfs:label "Laser cutting"@en ;
                                                                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A non-contact, thermal-based fabrication process for cutting materials." ;
                                                                 <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/definitionSource> "GPT-4 generated description with manual adjustments" .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/LatentHeatOfEvaporation
<https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/LatentHeatOfEvaporation> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                            rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/ThermalProperty> ;
                                                                            rdfs:label "Latent heat of evaporation"@en ;
                                                                            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The amount of energy required to convert a unit mass of a material from liquid to gas at constant temperature and pressure." ;
                                                                            <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/definitionSource> "GPT-4 generated description with manual adjustments" .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/LatticeParameter
<https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/LatticeParameter> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                     rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/MicrostructuralProperty> ;
                                                                     rdfs:label "Lattice parameter"@en ;
                                                                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A charactersitic length or angle within a unit cell of a specific crystal lattice system, defined by the Bravais lattices. The length typically define the spacing between atoms which are repeated periodically along specific crystallographic directions." ;
                                                                     <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/definitionSource> "GPT-4 generated description with manual adjustments" .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/LedeburiteI
<https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/LedeburiteI> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/Microstructure> ;
                                                                rdfs:label "Ledeburite I"@en ;
                                                                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An eutectic microstructure of steel at elevated temperature composed of austenite and cementite"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/LedeburiteII
<https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/LedeburiteII> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                 rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/Microstructure> ;
                                                                 rdfs:label "Ledeburite II"@en ;
                                                                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An eutectic microstructure of steel at elevated temperature composed of pearlite and cementite. Instead of pearlite, also bainite or martensite can be present when cooled faster."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/LightOpticalMicroscope
