                                                              <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/definitionSource> "Description generated by GPT-4" .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/LowcycleFatigue
<https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/LowcycleFatigue> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                    rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/Mechanism> ;
                                                                    rdfs:label "Low-cycle fatigue"@en ;
                                                                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "LCF conditions occur at higher applied stress amplitudes for which the cyclic plasticity becomes widespread and more homogeneously distributed. From a mechanics perspective, LCF can be regarded as an homogenization problem involving multisite cracking and coalescence. Variability of behavior in LCF is less pronounced for a givenmicrostructure and arises chiefly in relation to crack growth phenomena."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/LowcycleFatigueTest
<https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/LowcycleFatigueTest> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                        rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/FatigueTest> ;
                                                                        rdfs:label "Low-cycle fatigue test"@en ;
                                                                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A fatigue test performed at high and medium cyclic amplitudes corresponding to macroscopic plasticity to characterize a materials LCF behaviour."@en ;
                                                                        <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/abbreviation> "LCF"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/LüdersBand
<https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/LüdersBand> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                               rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/Damage> ;
                                                               rdfs:label "Lüders band"@en ;
                                                               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Strain localization phenomenon which results in band-shaped strain distribution and occurs during tensile deformation of many materials. The underlying mechanism is associated with dynamic strain aging, i.e. interstitial atoms, such as carbon in steels, which can inhibit dislocation motion." ;
                                                               <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/definitionSource> "GPT-4 generated description with manual adjustments" .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/MachiningProcess
<https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/MachiningProcess> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                     rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/ManufacturingProcess> ;
                                                                     rdfs:label "Machining process"@en ;
                                                                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A process in which a piece of raw material is abrasively processed into a desired final shape and size by a controlled material-removal process such as milling or turning." ;
                                                                     <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/definitionSource> "GPT-4 generated description with manual adjustments" .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/MacroscopicGrainBoundaryParameter
<https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/MacroscopicGrainBoundaryParameter> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                                      rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/MicrostructuralProperty> ;
                                                                                      rdfs:label "Macroscopic grain boundary parameter"@en ;
                                                                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A group of parameters that describe the structure of a grain boundary on a macroscopic level, specifically the misorientation across a grain boundary with three parameters (Rodrigues vector) and the orientation of the grain boundary plane normal with two parameters amounting to five parameters." ;
                                                                                      <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/definitionSource> "GPT-4 generated description with manual adjustments" .


