###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/PlasticStrainRatio
<https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/PlasticStrainRatio> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                       rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/MechanicalProperty> ;
                                                                       rdfs:label "Plastic strain ratio"@en ;
                                                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A measure of the resistance of sheet metal to thinning or thickening deformation when subjected to tensile or compressive strain. A high plastic strain ratio implies easily in-plane which is typically desirable to avoid stress concentrations." ;
                                                                       <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/definitionSource> "GPT-4 generated description with manual adjustments" .


