###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/RollingContactFatigueTest
<https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/RollingContactFatigueTest> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                              rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/FatigueTest> ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "Rolling contact fatigue test"@en ;
                                                                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Rolling contact fatigue (RCF) is defined as the process of fatigue due to rolling/sliding contact."@en ;
                                                                              <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/abbreviation> "RCF"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/Roughing
<https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/Roughing> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                             rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/MachiningProcess> ;
                                                             rdfs:label "Roughing"@en ;
                                                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Roughing cuts are used to remove large amount of material from the starting workpart as rapidly as possible, i.e. with a large Material Removal Rate (MRR), in order to produce a shape close to the desired form, but leaving some material on the piece for a subsequent finishing operation."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/materials-mechanics-ontology/RunOutFatigueSpecimen
